number   '5.2'     -> 5.2
number   'five'    -> REJECTED: expected number, got 'five'
boolean  'true'    -> True
boolean  'yes'     -> REJECTED: expected boolean, got 'yes'
string   123       -> REJECTED: expected string, got int

--- 3. Order matters: coerce first, then check the enum ---
'2' against enum [1,2,3] without coercion: False
