[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Role-Based Agent Teams: Tools, Typed Results and Memory (Part 2 of 3)","textKn":"ಪಾತ್ರ-ಆಧಾರಿತ Agent ತಂಡಗಳು: Tools, Typed ಫಲಿತಾಂಶಗಳು ಮತ್ತು Memory (ಭಾಗ 2 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 2 of 3: the @tool decorator, per-agent tool access, a typed ResearchResult and layered memory. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of CrewAI's ideas, not the CrewAI library, and the model is a deterministic stand-in, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The pasted Part 2 was a flattened export; the code is rebuilt from its descriptions. The retrieval used here is word overlap, a deliberately simple stand-in for embedding search. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 2ನೆಯದು: @tool decorator, ಪ್ರತಿ-agent tool ಪ್ರವೇಶ, typed ResearchResult ಮತ್ತು ಪದರಯುಕ್ತ memory. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು CrewAI ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, CrewAI ಲೈಬ್ರರಿ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದರಿ ನಿರ್ಧಾರಾತ್ಮಕ ಬದಲಿ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಅಂಟಿಸಿದ ಭಾಗ 2 ಚಪ್ಪಟೆಯಾದ ರಫ್ತು; ಕೋಡ್ ಅದರ ವಿವರಣೆಗಳಿಂದ ಮರುನಿರ್ಮಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ. ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಬಳಸಿದ ಹುಡುಕಾಟ ಪದ-ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣ, ಎಂಬೆಡಿಂಗ್ ಹುಡುಕಾಟಕ್ಕೆ ಉದ್ದೇಶಪೂರ್ವಕ ಸರಳ ಬದಲಿ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Reaching Outside the Prompt","textKn":"ಪ್ರಾಂಪ್ಟ್ ಹೊರಗೆ ತಲುಪುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Tools, Contracts and Memory","headingKn":"Tools, ಒಪ್ಪಂದಗಳು ಮತ್ತು Memory","bodyEn":"Part 1 left three gaps. An agent cannot act on the world, so it needs tools. Output shape is only requested, so it needs a typed result. And each run starts from nothing, so it needs memory. A tool is a named function plus a description a model can read; the docstring is that description, which makes it the interface. A typed result is a frozen dataclass that validates itself. Memory comes in layers: short-term for the current run, long-term for facts across runs, entity for facts about named things.","bodyKn":"ಭಾಗ 1 ಮೂರು ಅಂತರಗಳನ್ನು ಬಿಟ್ಟಿತು. Agent ಜಗತ್ತಿನ ಮೇಲೆ ಕ್ರಿಯೆ ಮಾಡಲಾರದು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ tools ಬೇಕು. Output ರೂಪ ಕೇವಲ ಕೋರಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿದೆ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ typed ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಬೇಕು. ಮತ್ತು ಪ್ರತಿ ಓಟ ಶೂನ್ಯದಿಂದ ಪ್ರಾರಂಭ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ memory ಬೇಕು. Tool ಎಂದರೆ ಹೆಸರಿಸಿದ ಕಾರ್ಯ ಜೊತೆ ಮಾದರಿ ಓದಬಹುದಾದ ವಿವರಣೆ; docstring ಆ ವಿವರಣೆ, ಅದನ್ನು ಇಂಟರ್ಫೇಸ್ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. Typed ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಸ್ವತಃ ಮಾನ್ಯ ಮಾಡುವ ಫ್ರೋಜನ್ dataclass. Memory ಪದರಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಬರುತ್ತದೆ: ಪ್ರಸ್ತುತ ಓಟಕ್ಕೆ ಅಲ್ಪಾವಧಿ, ಓಟಗಳಾದ್ಯಂತ ಸಂಗತಿಗಳಿಗೆ ದೀರ್ಘಾವಧಿ, ಹೆಸರಿಸಿದ ವಸ್ತುಗಳ ಸಂಗತಿಗಳಿಗೆ entity."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"An Agent With Tools, a Typed Result and Memory","headingKn":"Tools, Typed ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಮತ್ತು Memory ಇರುವ Agent","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">Tools, typed results and memory around an agent</text><rect x="100" y="28" width="100" height="38" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="150" y="43" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text><text x="150" y="55" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tools it was given</text><rect x="10" y="90" width="85" height="38" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="52.5" y="105" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text><text x="52.5" y="117" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">name + docstring</text><rect x="108" y="90" width="85" height="38" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150.5" y="105" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">ResearchResult</text><text x="150.5" y="117" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">typed, validated</text><rect x="205" y="90" width="85" height="38" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="247.5" y="105" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">Memory</text><text x="247.5" y="117" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">short/long/entity</text><path d="M130,66 L52,90 M150,66 V90 M170,66 L247,90" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">the docstring is the interface; the type is the contract</text></svg>","captionEn":"The docstring is the tool interface; the dataclass is the output contract.","captionKn":"Docstring tool ಇಂಟರ್ಫೇಸ್; dataclass output ಒಪ್ಪಂದ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"Memory layers in the lab","headingKn":"ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ memory ಪದರಗಳು","headers":["Layer","Holds","Lifetime"],"rows":[["short_term","What happened this run","One kickoff"],["long_term","Facts to retrieve later","Across kickoffs"],["entities","Facts keyed by a named thing","Across kickoffs"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building Them","textKn":"ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"crew_2.py","headingEn":"Tool, @tool, ToolAgent and the typed ResearchResult","headingKn":"Tool, @tool, ToolAgent ಮತ್ತು typed ResearchResult","descEn":"tool(name) turns a function into a Tool carrying its docstring as the description. pick_tool is a crude description-driven chooser. ToolAgent refuses tools it was not given. ResearchResult is frozen and validates itself in __post_init__; parse_result turns agent text into one.","descKn":"tool(name) ಕಾರ್ಯವನ್ನು ತನ್ನ docstring ಅನ್ನು ವಿವರಣೆಯಾಗಿ ಹೊತ್ತ Tool ಆಗಿ ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. pick_tool ವಿವರಣೆ-ಚಾಲಿತ ಒರಟು ಆಯ್ಕೆಗಾರ. ToolAgent ತನಗೆ ನೀಡದ tools ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ResearchResult ಫ್ರೋಜನ್ ಮತ್ತು __post_init__ ನಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ವತಃ ಮಾನ್ಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ; parse_result agent ಪಠ್ಯವನ್ನು ಒಂದಾಗಿ ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"@dataclass
class Tool:
    name: str
    description: str
    function: Callable

    def run(self, **kwargs):
        return self.function(**kwargs)


def tool(name: str):
    def decorator(func):
        return Tool(name=name, description=func.__doc__ or "", function=func)
    return decorator


@tool("search")
def search(query: str) -> str:
    """Search a deterministic local knowledge base."""
    kb = {"agent engineering": "Memory, tools and flows.", "crew": "A container of agents and tasks."}
    return kb.get(query.lower(), "no result")


@tool("calculator")
def calculator(expression: str) -> str:
    """Add two integers written like '2 + 3'."""
    a, b = expression.split("+")
    return str(int(a) + int(b))


@tool("word_count")
def word_count(text: str) -> str:
    return str(len(text.split()))


class ToolAgent(Agent):
    """An agent that may only call tools it was given."""

    def use(self, tool_name: str, **kwargs):
        allowed = {t.name: t for t in self.tools}
        if tool_name not in allowed:
            raise PermissionError(f"{self.role} has no tool {tool_name!r}; it has {sorted(allowed)}")
        return allowed[tool_name].run(**kwargs)


def pick_tool(tools, request: str):
    """Choose a tool by word overlap between the request and each description (a crude stand-in for a model reading them)."""
    words = set(request.lower().split())
    scored = sorted(((len(words & set(t.description.lower().split())), t.name) for t in tools), reverse=True)
    return scored[0]


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class ResearchResult:
    topic: str
    findings: tuple

    def __post_init__(self):
        if not self.topic:
            raise ValueError("topic must not be empty")
        if len(self.findings) != 3:
            raise ValueError(f"expected exactly 3 findings, got {len(self.findings)}")


def parse_result(topic: str, text: str) -> ResearchResult:
    lines = tuple(l.split(": ", 1)[1] for l in text.splitlines() if l.startswith("Finding") and ": " in l)
    return ResearchResult(topic, lines)"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"crew_2.py","headingEn":"Memory, MemoryCrew and main(): seven experiments","headingKn":"Memory, MemoryCrew ಮತ್ತು main(): ಏಳು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"Memory keeps the three layers and retrieves by word overlap with an optional stop-word list, k and min_score. MemoryCrew reads long-term memory before a run and writes the result back after it. main() checks tool description, per-agent access, typed rejection, retrieval failure modes and memory across two kickoffs.","descKn":"Memory ಮೂರು ಪದರಗಳನ್ನು ಇಟ್ಟು ಐಚ್ಛಿಕ stop-word ಪಟ್ಟಿ, k ಮತ್ತು min_score ಜೊತೆ ಪದ-ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣದಿಂದ ಹುಡುಕುತ್ತದೆ. MemoryCrew ಓಟದ ಮೊದಲು ದೀರ್ಘಾವಧಿ memory ಓದಿ ನಂತರ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಮರಳಿ ಬರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. main() tool ವಿವರಣೆ, ಪ್ರತಿ-agent ಪ್ರವೇಶ, typed ತಿರಸ್ಕಾರ, ಹುಡುಕಾಟ ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ವಿಧಾನಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡು kickoffs ಅಡ್ಡಲಾಗಿ memory ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"STOP = {"the", "a", "an", "is", "of", "and", "to", "in", "for", "what", "does"}


class Memory:
    def __init__(self, use_stopwords=False):
        self.short_term, self.long_term, self.entities = [], [], {}
        self.use_stopwords = use_stopwords

    def remember_short(self, value):
        self.short_term.append(value)

    def remember_long(self, value):
        self.long_term.append(value)

    def remember_entity(self, name, fact):
        self.entities.setdefault(name, []).append(fact)

    def _words(self, text):
        w = set(text.lower().replace("?", "").replace(".", "").split())
        return w - STOP if self.use_stopwords else w

    def retrieve(self, query, k=2, min_score=0):
        q = self._words(query)
        scored = sorted(((len(q & self._words(m)), m) for m in self.long_term), key=lambda x: -x[0])
        return [(s, m) for s, m in scored[:k] if s >= min_score]


class MemoryCrew:
    """Sequential crew whose first agent reads long-term memory and whose result is written back after the run."""

    def __init__(self, memory, use_memory=True):
        self.memory, self.use_memory = memory, use_memory

    def kickoff(self, topic):
        hits = self.memory.retrieve(topic, min_score=1) if self.use_memory else []
        context = topic + ("\nPRIOR: " + " | ".join(m for _, m in hits) if hits else "")
        crew = SequentialCrew([], [Task("Research", "three findings", Agent("Researcher", "g", "b"))])
        out, _ = crew.kickoff(context)
        self.memory.remember_long(f"{topic}: {out.splitlines()[0]}")
        return context, hits


def section(t):
    print(f"\n--- {t} ---")


def main():
    section("1. The @tool decorator turns a function into a described object")
    for t in (search, calculator, word_count):
        print(f"{t.name!r}: description={t.description!r}")
    print("search(agent engineering) ->", search.run(query="agent engineering"))
    print("calculator('2 + 3') ->", calculator.run(expression="2 + 3"))

    section("2. Genuinely checking: a tool with no docstring has nothing for a model to read")
    tools = [search, calculator, word_count]
    for request in ("search the knowledge base for crew", "add two integers", "count the words in this text"):
        score, name = pick_tool(tools, request)
        words = set(request.lower().split())
        allscores = {t.name: len(words & set(t.description.lower().split())) for t in tools}
        print(f"request {request!r:42} -> picked {name!r}; scores {allscores}")
    print("the word-count request scores 0 for every tool, so 'word_count' was chosen only by the sort tie-break, not by evidence")
    print("an empty description can never earn a positive score, so a description-driven chooser cannot select it on merit")

    section("3. Tool access is per agent")
    r = ToolAgent("Researcher", "g", "b", tools=[search])
    print("researcher uses search:", r.use("search", query="crew"))
    try:
        r.use("calculator", expression="1 + 1")
    except PermissionError as e:
        print("PermissionError:", e)
    try:
        r.use("search", wrong_argument="x")
    except TypeError as e:
        print("TypeError:", e)
    try:
        calculator.run(expression="2 plus 3")
    except ValueError as e:
        print("tool body error surfaces as:", type(e).__name__, "-", e)

    section("4. Genuinely checking: structured output rejects what expected_output would accept")
    good = "Finding 1: a\nFinding 2: b\nFinding 3: c"
    print("good ->", parse_result("agents", good))
    for label, text in (("two findings", "Finding 1: a\nFinding 2: b"),
                        ("prose", "Here are my thoughts on agents, they are great."),
                        ("four findings", good + "\nFinding 4: d")):
        try:
            parse_result("agents", text)
        except ValueError as e:
            print(f"{label:14} -> ValueError: {e}")
    try:
        parse_result("agents", good).topic = "x"
    except Exception as e:
        print("the typed result is frozen:", type(e).__name__)
    print("note: 3 findings of nonsense still pass; a typed shape checks structure, not truth")
    print("nonsense passes:", parse_result("agents", "Finding 1: ?\nFinding 2: ?\nFinding 3: ?").findings)

    section("5. Layers of memory")
    m = Memory()
    m.remember_short("user asked about CrewAI")
    m.remember_long("Flows give deterministic control of a pipeline")
    m.remember_long("Crews give role-based collaboration")
    m.remember_long("Process decides the execution strategy of a crew")
    m.remember_entity("CrewAI", "a framework for role-based agents")
    print("short:", m.short_term, "| entities:", m.entities)
    print("retrieve('what is a Process'):", m.retrieve("what is a Process", k=2))

    section("6. Genuinely checking: word-overlap retrieval and its failure modes")
    raw, filt = Memory(), Memory(use_stopwords=True)
    for mem in (raw, filt):
        mem.remember_long("the team decided to ship on Friday")
        mem.remember_long("the deadline for the release is Friday")
        mem.remember_long("tea is served in the afternoon")
    q = "what is the plan for the launch"
    print("query:", q)
    print("raw words        :", raw.retrieve(q, k=1))
    print("stop-words dropped:", filt.retrieve(q, k=1))
    print("paraphrase 'when do we release' ->", filt.retrieve("when do we release", k=2))
    print("zero-overlap top-k still returns items unless min_score is set:", filt.retrieve("zzz unrelated", k=2))
    print("with min_score=1:", filt.retrieve("zzz unrelated", k=2, min_score=1))

    section("7. Genuinely checking: memory across two kickoffs")
    for use in (False, True):
        mem = Memory(use_stopwords=True)
        crew = MemoryCrew(mem, use_memory=use)
        crew.kickoff("agent engineering")
        context, hits = crew.kickoff("agent engineering")
        print(f"use_memory={use}: second-run context has prior knowledge = {'PRIOR' in context}; long-term items = {len(mem.long_term)}")
    mem = Memory(use_stopwords=True)
    mem.remember_long("pricing: the plan costs 10 dollars")
    mem.remember_long("pricing: the plan now costs 20 dollars")
    print("two contradicting facts both come back:", [x for _, x in mem.retrieve("pricing plan costs", k=2)])
    print("retrieval returns what matches, not what is currently true")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
