[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Role-Based Agent Teams: Flows and the Complete System (Part 3 of 3)","textKn":"ಪಾತ್ರ-ಆಧಾರಿತ Agent ತಂಡಗಳು: Flows ಮತ್ತು ಸಂಪೂರ್ಣ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ (ಭಾಗ 3 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 3 of 3: event-driven Flows, a Crew inside a Flow, Flow failure modes and a measured crew-versus-flow comparison. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of CrewAI's ideas, not the CrewAI library, and the model is a deterministic stand-in, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The pasted Part 3 was a flattened export whose final program was cut off, so the system here is rebuilt. Section 6 uses a simulated 15 percent mis-route rate that is an assumption, not a measurement of any real model. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 3ನೆಯದು: ಘಟನೆ-ಚಾಲಿತ Flows, Flow ಒಳಗೆ Crew, Flow ವೈಫಲ್ಯ ವಿಧಾನಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಅಳೆದ crew-ವರ್ಸಸ್-flow ಹೋಲಿಕೆ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು CrewAI ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, CrewAI ಲೈಬ್ರರಿ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದರಿ ನಿರ್ಧಾರಾತ್ಮಕ ಬದಲಿ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಅಂಟಿಸಿದ ಭಾಗ 3 ಚಪ್ಪಟೆಯಾದ ರಫ್ತು ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ಅಂತಿಮ ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತ್ತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಇಲ್ಲಿನ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಮರುನಿರ್ಮಿತ. ವಿಭಾಗ 6 ಸಿಮ್ಯುಲೇಟೆಡ್ 15 ಶೇಕಡಾ ತಪ್ಪು-ಮಾರ್ಗ ದರ ಬಳಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಅದು ಊಹೆ, ಯಾವುದೇ ನಿಜವಾದ ಮಾದರಿಯ ಅಳತೆ ಅಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Control Plane Versus Intelligence","textKn":"ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ ಸಮತಲ ಮತ್ತು ಬುದ್ಧಿವಂತಿಕೆ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Crew for Exploration, Flow for Control","headingKn":"ಅನ್ವೇಷಣೆಗೆ Crew, ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣಕ್ಕೆ Flow","bodyEn":"A Crew gives role-based collaboration where the model decides how to approach the work. A Flow gives an explicit event-driven path: one @start method, methods that @listen for named events, each returning an (event, payload) pair. The two compose: a Flow owns control, and one of its steps can be a Crew for the open-ended part. The Flow engine here is about forty lines: decorators only attach metadata, and a runner reads it.","bodyKn":"Crew ಮಾದರಿ ಕೆಲಸವನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ಸಮೀಪಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುವಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾತ್ರ-ಆಧಾರಿತ ಸಹಕಾರ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ. Flow ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟ ಘಟನೆ-ಚಾಲಿತ ಮಾರ್ಗ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ: ಒಂದು @start ವಿಧಾನ, ಹೆಸರಿಸಿದ ಘಟನೆಗಳಿಗೆ @listen ಮಾಡುವ ವಿಧಾನಗಳು, ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದೂ (event, payload) ಜೋಡಿ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಎರಡೂ ಸೇರಬಹುದು: Flow ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ ಹೊಂದಿದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ಒಂದು ಹಂತ ಮುಕ್ತ ಭಾಗಕ್ಕೆ Crew ಆಗಬಹುದು. ಇಲ್ಲಿನ Flow ಎಂಜಿನ್ ಸುಮಾರು ನಲವತ್ತು ಸಾಲು: decorators ಕೇವಲ ಮೆಟಾಡೇಟಾ ಅಂಟಿಸುತ್ತವೆ, ಮತ್ತು runner ಅದನ್ನು ಓದುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"A Flow With a Crew Step","headingKn":"Crew ಹಂತ ಇರುವ Flow","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">Flow controls the path; a Crew can be one step</text><rect x="10" y="40" width="70" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="45" y="55" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">@start</text><text x="45" y="67" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">research</text><rect x="115" y="40" width="70" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="150" y="55" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">@listen</text><text x="150" y="67" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">crew_step</text><rect x="220" y="40" width="70" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="255" y="55" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">@listen</text><text x="255" y="67" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">publish</text><path d="M80,57 H115 M185,57 H220" stroke="#475569"/><text x="97" y="52" fill="#94a3b8" font-size="6">ready</text><text x="202" y="52" fill="#94a3b8" font-size="6">crewed</text><rect x="100" y="105" width="100" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="120" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">Crew inside</text><text x="150" y="132" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">open-ended work</text><path d="M150,74 V105" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">events name the edges, so the path is inspectable and replayable</text></svg>","captionEn":"Events name the edges of the path, so the whole run can be traced and replayed.","captionKn":"ಘಟನೆಗಳು ಮಾರ್ಗದ ಅಂಚುಗಳಿಗೆ ಹೆಸರಿಡುತ್ತವೆ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಇಡೀ ಓಟ ಅನುಸರಿಸಿ ಮರುಚಲಾಯಿಸಬಹುದು."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"Crew versus Flow","headingKn":"Crew ಮತ್ತು Flow ಹೋಲಿಕೆ","headers":["","Crew","Flow"],"rows":[["Path decided by","Roles and a manager","Named events in code"],["Strength","Exploratory collaboration","Replay, audit, testing"],["Risk","Skipped or reordered steps","Silent dead ends from bad event names"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building the Flow and the System","textKn":"Flow ಮತ್ತು ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"crew_3.py","headingEn":"@start, @listen, FlowRunner and two example flows","headingKn":"@start, @listen, FlowRunner ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡು ಉದಾಹರಣೆ flows","descEn":"start and listen only set attributes. FlowRunner finds the single start method, then repeatedly finds the one listener for the last event, calling it with the payload. It raises if there are zero start methods, several listeners for one event, or too many steps; an event with no listener ends the run and is recorded in unhandled. CrewInFlow calls a sequential crew from inside one step.","descKn":"start ಮತ್ತು listen ಕೇವಲ ಗುಣಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನು ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತವೆ. FlowRunner ಏಕೈಕ start ವಿಧಾನ ಕಂಡುಹಿಡಿದು, ನಂತರ ಕೊನೆಯ ಘಟನೆಗೆ ಏಕೈಕ listener ಕಂಡುಹಿಡಿದು payload ಜೊತೆ ಕರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಶೂನ್ಯ start ವಿಧಾನಗಳು, ಒಂದು ಘಟನೆಗೆ ಹಲವು listeners ಅಥವಾ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಹಂತಗಳಿದ್ದರೆ ಅದು ಎತ್ತುತ್ತದೆ; listener ಇಲ್ಲದ ಘಟನೆ ಓಟ ಕೊನೆಗೊಳಿಸಿ unhandled ನಲ್ಲಿ ದಾಖಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ. CrewInFlow ಒಂದು ಹಂತದೊಳಗಿಂದ sequential crew ಕರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def start(func):
    func._is_start = True
    return func


def listen(topic):
    def decorator(func):
        func._listens_to = topic
        return func
    return decorator


class FlowRunner:
    def __init__(self, flow, max_steps=20):
        self.flow, self.max_steps = flow, max_steps
        self.trace, self.unhandled = [], []

    def _methods(self):
        return [(n, getattr(self.flow, n)) for n in dir(self.flow) if callable(getattr(self.flow, n)) and not n.startswith("_")]

    def run(self, initial_input):
        starts = [f for _, f in self._methods() if getattr(f, "_is_start", False)]
        if len(starts) != 1:
            raise ValueError(f"a flow needs exactly one @start method, found {len(starts)}")
        event, payload = starts[0](initial_input)
        self.trace.append((starts[0].__name__, event))
        for _ in range(self.max_steps):
            listeners = [f for _, f in self._methods() if getattr(f, "_listens_to", None) == event]
            if not listeners:
                self.unhandled.append(event)
                return event, payload
            if len(listeners) > 1:
                raise ValueError(f"event {event!r} has {len(listeners)} listeners: {[f.__name__ for f in listeners]}")
            event, payload = listeners[0](payload)
            self.trace.append((listeners[0].__name__, event))
        raise RuntimeError(f"flow exceeded {self.max_steps} steps; trace tail: {self.trace[-3:]}")


class BriefFlow:
    @start
    def research(self, topic):
        return "researched", f"Research completed for {topic}"

    @listen("researched")
    def write(self, research):
        return "drafted", f"Draft based on: {research}"

    @listen("drafted")
    def edit(self, draft):
        return "edited", f"Edited version: {draft}"


class CrewInFlow:
    """A Flow whose middle step delegates to a Crew; the Flow owns control, the Crew owns the open-ended part."""

    @start
    def gather(self, topic):
        return "ready", (topic, search.run(query=topic))

    @listen("ready")
    def crew_step(self, payload):
        topic, fact = payload
        crew = SequentialCrew([researcher, writer, editor], [
            Task("Research.", "three findings", researcher),
            Task("Write.", "one sentence", writer),
            Task("Edit.", "one sentence", editor),
        ])
        result, _ = crew.kickoff(f"{topic}: {fact}")
        return "crewed", result

    @listen("crewed")
    def publish(self, text):
        return "published", f"PUBLISHED: {text}""}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"crew_3.py","headingEn":"Broken flows, a noisy manager and main(): six experiments","headingKn":"ಮುರಿದ flows, ಗದ್ದಲದ ಮ್ಯಾನೇಜರ್ ಮತ್ತು main(): ಆರು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"TypoFlow listens for a misspelled event, DuplicateFlow has two listeners, LoopFlow cycles. noisy_manager mis-routes with probability 0.15 using a seeded generator. main() runs all six experiments, including the 200-seed comparison.","descKn":"TypoFlow ತಪ್ಪಾಗಿ ಬರೆದ ಘಟನೆಗೆ ಕಾಯುತ್ತದೆ, DuplicateFlow ಗೆ ಎರಡು listeners ಇವೆ, LoopFlow ಚಕ್ರ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. noisy_manager ಬೀಜ ಹಾಕಿದ ಜನರೇಟರ್‌ನಿಂದ 0.15 ಸಂಭವನೀಯತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತಪ್ಪು ಮಾರ್ಗ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. main() 200-ಬೀಜ ಹೋಲಿಕೆ ಸೇರಿ ಎಲ್ಲ ಆರು ಪ್ರಯೋಗ ಚಲಾಯಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class TypoFlow:
    @start
    def research(self, topic):
        return "researched", topic

    @listen("reserched")
    def write(self, x):
        return "drafted", x


class DuplicateFlow:
    @start
    def a(self, x):
        return "go", x

    @listen("go")
    def b(self, x):
        return "b-done", x

    @listen("go")
    def c(self, x):
        return "c-done", x


class LoopFlow:
    @start
    def a(self, x):
        return "ping", x

    @listen("ping")
    def b(self, x):
        return "pong", x

    @listen("pong")
    def c(self, x):
        return "ping", x


def section(t):
    print(f"\n--- {t} ---")


def noisy_manager(rng):
    """A routing manager with a small chance of a wrong pick, standing in for model variance (a simulation, not a measurement of any real LLM)."""
    def choose(context, completed):
        for role in ("Researcher", "Writer", "Editor"):
            if role not in completed:
                return rng.choice(["Writer", "Editor", "Researcher"]) if rng.random() < 0.15 else role
        return "done"
    return choose


def main():
    section("1. A Flow: decorators attach metadata, the runner reads it")
    flow = BriefFlow()
    print("research is_start:", getattr(flow.research, "_is_start", False), "| write listens to:", flow.write._listens_to)
    runner = FlowRunner(flow)
    event, payload = runner.run("agent engineering")
    for step, ev in runner.trace:
        print(f"{step} -> emits {ev!r}")
    print("final:", event, "|", payload)

    section("2. A Crew inside a Flow")
    r2 = FlowRunner(CrewInFlow())
    event, payload = r2.run("agent engineering")
    print("steps:", [s for s, _ in r2.trace])
    print("final:", payload)

    section("3. Genuinely checking: a misspelled event name ends the flow silently")
    r3 = FlowRunner(TypoFlow())
    event, payload = r3.run("agent engineering")
    print("trace:", r3.trace, "| returned event:", repr(event), "| unhandled:", r3.unhandled)
    print("no exception: 'write' never ran and the caller got a perfectly normal-looking return value")

    section("4. Genuinely checking: two listeners, and a cycle")
    try:
        FlowRunner(DuplicateFlow()).run("x")
    except ValueError as e:
        print("ValueError:", e)
    try:
        FlowRunner(LoopFlow(), max_steps=10).run("x")
    except RuntimeError as e:
        print("RuntimeError:", e)

    section("5. The complete system: tool + crew + typed result + assertions")
    topic = "agent engineering"
    fact = search.run(query=topic)
    crew_text = "Finding 1: " + fact.rstrip(".") + "\nFinding 2: Flows give control\nFinding 3: Crews give roles"
    result = parse_result(topic, crew_text)
    assert isinstance(result, ResearchResult) and len(result.findings) == 3
    print("typed handoff:", result)
    first, _ = SequentialCrew([researcher, writer, editor], [Task("R", "o", researcher), Task("W", "o", writer), Task("E", "o", editor)]).kickoff(topic)
    second, _ = SequentialCrew([researcher, writer, editor], [Task("R", "o", researcher), Task("W", "o", writer), Task("E", "o", editor)]).kickoff(topic)
    print("two identical runs give identical text:", first == second)
    print("all assertions passed")

    section("6. Genuinely measuring: free-routing crew vs Flow, 200 seeds with a simulated 15% mis-route")
    intended = ("manager->Researcher", "manager->Writer", "manager->Editor", "manager->done")
    outcomes, distinct = Counter(), set()
    for seed in range(200):
        crew = HierarchicalCrew([researcher, writer, editor], noisy_manager(random.Random(seed)), max_steps=12)
        text, trace = crew.kickoff(topic)
        distinct.add(tuple(trace))
        outcomes["intended order" if tuple(trace) == intended else "finished, but a role was skipped or reordered"] += 1
    print("noisy manager outcomes:", dict(outcomes), "| distinct traces:", len(distinct))
    flow_outputs = {FlowRunner(BriefFlow()).run(topic)[1] for _ in range(200)}
    print("Flow over 200 runs: distinct final outputs =", len(flow_outputs))
    print("none of the 200 crew runs raised an error, so the wrong-order runs are invisible unless you inspect the trace")
    print("the 15% is an assumption, so the exact counts are illustrative; the structural point is that a decision per step is a failure point per step")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
