[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Agent Benchmarks: SWE-bench, GAIA and AgentBench (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"Agent Benchmarks: SWE-bench, GAIA ಮತ್ತು AgentBench (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: a SWE-bench-style evaluator with FAIL_TO_PASS and PASS_TO_PASS gates. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind SWE-bench, GAIA and AgentBench, not the real software, and candidate patches, agents and models are scripted stand-ins, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The pasted Part 1 was cut off in the middle of its program, so the evaluator is rebuilt. No real SWE-bench task, repository or published result is used. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: FAIL_TO_PASS ಮತ್ತು PASS_TO_PASS ಗೇಟ್‌ಗಳಿರುವ SWE-bench-ಶೈಲಿಯ evaluator. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು SWE-bench, GAIA ಮತ್ತು AgentBench ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಅಭ್ಯರ್ಥಿ patches, agents ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದರಿಗಳು ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಬದಲಿಗಳು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಅಂಟಿಸಿದ ಭಾಗ 1 ತನ್ನ ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ ಮಧ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತ್ತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ evaluator ಮರುನಿರ್ಮಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ. ಯಾವುದೇ ನಿಜ SWE-bench ಕಾರ್ಯ, repository ಅಥವಾ ಪ್ರಕಟಿತ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶ ಬಳಸಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"A Benchmark Needs an Evaluator","textKn":"Benchmark ಗೆ evaluator ಬೇಕು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Repository, Issue, Patch, Tests","headingKn":"Repository, Issue, Patch, Tests","bodyEn":"A SWE-bench task gives an agent a repository and an issue, and asks for a patch. The patch is judged by running tests, not by reading it. FAIL_TO_PASS tests fail before the fix and must pass after it (the bug gate). PASS_TO_PASS tests pass before and must still pass (the regression gate). A task is resolved only if both sets are fully green. Execution is stronger than comparing text with the human patch, but it can only be as strong as the tests, which is what this lab probes.","bodyKn":"SWE-bench ಕಾರ್ಯ agent ಗೆ repository ಮತ್ತು issue ನೀಡಿ patch ಕೇಳುತ್ತದೆ. Patch ಅನ್ನು ಓದಿ ಅಲ್ಲ, tests ಚಲಾಯಿಸಿ ತೀರ್ಮಾನಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ. FAIL_TO_PASS tests ಸರಿಪಡಿಸುವ ಮುನ್ನ ವಿಫಲವಾಗಿ ನಂತರ ಪಾಸ್ ಆಗಬೇಕು (ದೋಷ ಗೇಟ್). PASS_TO_PASS tests ಮೊದಲು ಪಾಸ್ ಆಗಿ ಈಗಲೂ ಪಾಸ್ ಆಗಬೇಕು (ಹಿಂಜರಿತ ಗೇಟ್). ಎರಡೂ ಗುಂಪುಗಳು ಸಂಪೂರ್ಣ ಹಸಿರಾದರೆ ಮಾತ್ರ ಕಾರ್ಯ resolved. ಮಾನವ patch ಜೊತೆ ಪಠ್ಯ ಹೋಲಿಕೆಗಿಂತ ಚಲಾವಣೆ ಬಲಿಷ್ಠ, ಆದರೆ ಅದು tests ಷ್ಟೇ ಬಲಿಷ್ಠ, ಈ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಅದನ್ನೇ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"The Two Gates","headingKn":"ಎರಡು ಗೇಟ್‌ಗಳು","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">Two gates decide whether a patch resolves a task</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">issue + repo</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">the task</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">candidate patch</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">from the agent</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">run tests</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">execution, not text</text><rect x="40" y="110" width="100" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="90" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">FAIL_TO_PASS</text><text x="90" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">the bug must be fixed</text><rect x="160" y="110" width="100" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="210" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">PASS_TO_PASS</text><text x="210" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">nothing else may break</text><path d="M90,47 H110 M190,47 H210 M250,64 L100,110 M250,64 L210,110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">resolved only if both gates are fully green</text></svg>","captionEn":"Both gates must be fully green for a task to count as resolved.","captionKn":"ಕಾರ್ಯ resolved ಎಂದು ಪರಿಗಣಿಸಲು ಎರಡೂ ಗೇಟ್‌ಗಳು ಸಂಪೂರ್ಣ ಹಸಿರಾಗಬೇಕು."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The two test sets","headingKn":"ಎರಡು ಟೆಸ್ಟ್ ಗುಂಪುಗಳು","headers":["","FAIL_TO_PASS","PASS_TO_PASS"],"rows":[["Before the patch","fails","passes"],["After a correct patch","passes","still passes"],["What it guards","the bug is fixed","nothing else broke"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building the Evaluator","textKn":"Evaluator ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"bench_1.py","headingEn":"TestCase, BenchmarkTask, run_test and evaluate","headingKn":"TestCase, BenchmarkTask, run_test ಮತ್ತು evaluate","descEn":"Tests store inputs and expected values, not code. run_test turns an exception into a failed result instead of crashing the evaluator. evaluate runs both gates and returns resolved plus the two pass counts. The toy bug is buggy_add, which subtracts when b is negative.","descKn":"Tests ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ನಿರೀಕ್ಷಿತ ಮೌಲ್ಯಗಳನ್ನು ಇಡುತ್ತವೆ, ಕೋಡ್ ಅಲ್ಲ. run_test exception ಅನ್ನು evaluator ಕುಸಿಸದೆ ವಿಫಲ ಫಲಿತಾಂಶವಾಗಿ ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. evaluate ಎರಡೂ ಗೇಟ್‌ಗಳನ್ನು ಚಲಾಯಿಸಿ resolved ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡು ಪಾಸ್ ಎಣಿಕೆಗಳನ್ನು ಮರಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಆಟಿಕೆ ದೋಷ buggy_add, ಇದು b ಋಣಾತ್ಮಕವಾದಾಗ ಕಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"@dataclass
class TestCase:
    name: str
    args: Tuple[Any, ...]
    expected: Any


@dataclass
class TestResult:
    name: str
    passed: bool
    detail: str


@dataclass
class BenchmarkTask:
    task_id: str
    title: str
    buggy_function: Callable
    fail_to_pass: List[TestCase]
    pass_to_pass: List[TestCase]


def buggy_add(a, b):
    if b < 0:
        return a - b
    return a + b


def patched_add(a, b):
    return a + b


def run_test(function, test):
    try:
        got = function(*test.args)
    except Exception as e:
        return TestResult(test.name, False, f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}")
    return TestResult(test.name, got == test.expected, f"got {got!r}, expected {test.expected!r}")


def evaluate(task, candidate):
    f2p = [run_test(candidate, t) for t in task.fail_to_pass]
    p2p = [run_test(candidate, t) for t in task.pass_to_pass]
    return {"resolved": all(r.passed for r in f2p) and all(r.passed for r in p2p),
            "f2p": f"{sum(r.passed for r in f2p)}/{len(f2p)}", "p2p": f"{sum(r.passed for r in p2p)}/{len(p2p)}"}"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"bench_1.py","headingEn":"Candidate patches, timeout runner and main()","headingKn":"ಅಭ್ಯರ್ಥಿ patches, timeout runner ಮತ್ತು main()","descEn":"Candidates include a correct patch, a no-op, a hard-coded one, an int-only cast, a crash, a flaky patch and an infinite loop. mutants() builds six single-edit variants to score the suite. evaluate_with_timeout runs a candidate in a child process so the evaluator can kill it.","descKn":"ಅಭ್ಯರ್ಥಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಸರಿಯಾದ patch, no-op, hard-coded, int-ಮಾತ್ರ cast, ಕುಸಿತ, flaky patch ಮತ್ತು ಅನಂತ ಲೂಪ್ ಇವೆ. mutants() suite ಗೆ ಅಂಕ ನೀಡಲು ಆರು ಒಂದೇ-ಸಂಪಾದನೆ ರೂಪಾಂತರಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. evaluate_with_timeout ಅಭ್ಯರ್ಥಿಯನ್ನು ಮಗು process ನಲ್ಲಿ ಚಲಾಯಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಇದರಿಂದ evaluator ಅದನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಬಹುದು.","code":"TASK = BenchmarkTask("toy-001", "add() mishandles negative b", buggy_add,
                     [TestCase("neg_b", (5, -3), 2)],
                     [TestCase("pos", (2, 3), 5), TestCase("zero", (4, 0), 4)])

STRONG_P2P = TASK.pass_to_pass + [TestCase("neg_a", (-4, 3), -1), TestCase("both_neg", (-2, -5), -7), TestCase("float", (0.5, 0.25), 0.75),
                                  TestCase("str", ("a", "b"), "ab"), TestCase("big", (10 ** 12, 1), 10 ** 12 + 1)]


def hardcoded(a, b):
    return 2 if (a, b) == (5, -3) else buggy_add(a, b)


def no_op(a, b):
    return buggy_add(a, b)


def int_only(a, b):
    return int(a) + int(b)


def always_five(a, b):
    return 5


def crashing(a, b):
    raise ValueError("patch does not apply")


def flaky(a, b):
    return a + b if random.random() < 0.8 else a - b


def spin(a, b):
    while True:
        pass


def _child(fn, task, q):
    q.put(evaluate(task, fn))


def evaluate_with_timeout(task, fn, seconds):
    q = mp.Queue()
    p = mp.Process(target=_child, args=(fn, task, q))
    t0 = time.perf_counter()
    p.start()
    p.join(seconds)
    if p.is_alive():
        p.terminate(); p.join()
        return {"resolved": False, "detail": f"killed after {time.perf_counter() - t0:.1f}s timeout"}
    return q.get()


def mutants():
    """Six single-edit variants of the correct function; a good suite should reject all of them."""
    return {
        "a - b": lambda a, b: a - b, "a * b": lambda a, b: a * b, "a + b + 1": lambda a, b: a + b + 1,
        "abs(b) added": lambda a, b: a + abs(b), "b<0 -> a-b (original bug)": buggy_add, "int() cast": int_only,
    }


def section(t):
    print(f"\n--- {t} ---")


def main():
    section("1. The two gates")
    print("buggy :", evaluate(TASK, buggy_add))
    print("fixed :", evaluate(TASK, patched_add))
    print("buggy fails FAIL_TO_PASS (it reproduces the bug) and passes PASS_TO_PASS; the fix passes both")

    section("2. Genuinely checking: candidates that satisfy the gates in the wrong way (3 visible tests)")
    cands = {"correct patch": patched_add, "no-op": no_op, "hard-coded test input": hardcoded, "always returns 5": always_five,
             "int-only cast": int_only, "crashes": crashing}
    for name, fn in cands.items():
        print(f"{name:22} {evaluate(TASK, fn)}")
    print("'hard-coded test input' resolved the task without fixing the bug, and 'int-only cast' resolved it while breaking floats and strings")

    section("3. Genuinely checking: the same candidates against a stronger PASS_TO_PASS suite")
    strong = BenchmarkTask("toy-001+", TASK.title, buggy_add, TASK.fail_to_pass, STRONG_P2P)
    for name, fn in cands.items():
        print(f"{name:22} {evaluate(strong, fn)}")
    print("adding 5 regression tests rejected both: the int-only patch broke the float and string cases, and the hard-coded patch still contained the original bug for (-2,-5) and for strings, which the new tests exercised; a hard-coded fix survives only while the suite never touches the same defect again")

    section("4. Genuinely measuring: how strong is each test suite (mutation score)")
    for label, task in (("3 tests (original)", TASK), ("8 tests (stronger)", strong)):
        muts = mutants()
        killed = [n for n, fn in muts.items() if not evaluate(task, fn)["resolved"]]
        print(f"{label:20} mutants rejected {len(killed)}/{len(muts)} | survived: {[n for n in muts if n not in killed]}")
    print("a resolved patch means 'passed these tests', and the suite's mutation score says how much that is worth")

    section("5. Genuinely checking: text comparison with a human patch versus execution")
    human = "def add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n"
    agent = "def add(a, b):\n    result = a + b\n    return result\n"
    ns1, ns2 = {}, {}
    exec(human, ns1); exec(agent, ns2)
    print("source strings equal:", human == agent, "| behaviour on the tests:", evaluate(TASK, ns2["add"])["resolved"])
    wrong = "def add(a, b):\n    return a+b  # same logic, different spacing\n"
    print("whitespace-only variant equal to human text:", wrong == human)
    print("string matching rejects a correct patch; execution accepts it")

    section("6. Genuinely measuring: a flaky candidate (passes ~80 percent per call)")
    random.seed(3)
    outcomes = [evaluate(TASK, flaky)["resolved"] for _ in range(1000)]
    print(f"resolved in {sum(outcomes)} of 1000 evaluations ({sum(outcomes) / 10:.1f} percent)")
    print("the expected rate is 0.8^2 = 64 percent, not 0.8^3, because the (4, 0) test passes whichever branch runs; a single run is not a verdict, so evaluators rerun or require determinism")

    section("7. Genuinely checking: a patch that never returns")
    r = evaluate_with_timeout(TASK, spin, 1.0)
    print("spin():", r)
    print("without a timeout the evaluator itself would hang; a child process lets it kill the candidate")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
