[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Agent Instructions as Executable Constraints (Part 2 of 3)","textKn":"Agent ಸೂಚನೆಗಳು ಕಾರ್ಯಗತಗೊಳಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ನಿರ್ಬಂಧಗಳಾಗಿ (ಭಾಗ 2 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 2 of 3: attacking the checkers: path spellings, stale test evidence, approval timing, uncertainty and the severity source. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind agent instructions as executable constraints (rule files, checkers, severities and gates), not the real software, and the run records are hand-written and no language model is involved, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The pasted source for this part never arrived (only Parts 1 and 3 were supplied), so it is built from the other two parts and the lesson outline, and the original program was not supplied either. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 2ನೆಯದು: checkers ಮೇಲೆ ದಾಳಿ: path ಕಾಗುಣಿತಗಳು, ಹಳೆಯ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಾ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಸಮಯ, ಅನಿಶ್ಚಿತತೆ ಮತ್ತು ತೀವ್ರತೆಯ ಮೂಲ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು agent ಸೂಚನೆಗಳು ಕಾರ್ಯಗತಗೊಳಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ನಿರ್ಬಂಧಗಳಾಗಿ (ನಿಯಮ ಫೈಲ್‌ಗಳು, checkers, ತೀವ್ರತೆಗಳು ಮತ್ತು gates) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು run ದಾಖಲೆಗಳು ಕೈಬರಹ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದೇ ಭಾಷಾ ಮಾದರಿ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ ಭಾಗದ ಅಂಟಿಸಿದ ಮೂಲ ಎಂದೂ ಬರಲಿಲ್ಲ (ಭಾಗ 1 ಮತ್ತು 3 ಮಾತ್ರ ಒದಗಿಸಲಾಗಿತ್ತು), ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಅದು ಇತರ ಎರಡು ಭಾಗಗಳು ಮತ್ತು lesson ರೂಪರೇಖೆಯಿಂದ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಮೂಲ ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ ಕೂಡ ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Checkers Are Software Too","textKn":"Checkers ಕೂಡ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Naive Rules and Their Fixes","headingKn":"ಸರಳ ನಿಯಮಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಅವುಗಳ ಪರಿಹಾರಗಳು","bodyEn":"A checker proves only the claim it evaluates. This part writes a simple version and a stronger version of four checkers and tries them on inputs they were not designed for: nine spellings of a protected path, a green test run from before the last edit, approvals that came late or named another target, uncertainty compared as strings, and a severity table the agent can edit.","bodyKn":"Checker ತಾನು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಮಾಡುವ ಹೇಳಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ಸಾಬೀತುಪಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಈ ಭಾಗ ನಾಲ್ಕು checkers ನ ಸರಳ ಮತ್ತು ಬಲವಾದ ಆವೃತ್ತಿ ಬರೆದು ಅವು ವಿನ್ಯಾಸಗೊಳ್ಳದ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತದೆ: ರಕ್ಷಿತ path ನ ಒಂಬತ್ತು ಕಾಗುಣಿತಗಳು, ಕೊನೆಯ ಸಂಪಾದನೆಗಿಂತ ಮುನ್ನದ ಹಸಿರು ಪರೀಕ್ಷಾ ಓಟ, ತಡವಾಗಿ ಬಂದ ಅಥವಾ ಬೇರೆ ಗುರಿ ಹೆಸರಿಸಿದ ಅನುಮೋದನೆಗಳು, ಸ್ಟ್ರಿಂಗ್ ಆಗಿ ಹೋಲಿಸಿದ ಅನಿಶ್ಚಿತತೆ ಮತ್ತು agent ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ತೀವ್ರತೆ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Every Checker Has Blind Spots","headingKn":"ಪ್ರತಿ Checker ಗೂ ಕುರುಡು ಬಿಂದುಗಳಿವೆ","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">Attacking the checkers</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">paths</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">spellings</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">tests</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">which revision</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">approval</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">when, for what</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">severity source</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">trusted file only</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">every checker has inputs it was not written for</text></svg>","captionEn":"Probe each rule with inputs it was not written for.","captionKn":"ಪ್ರತಿ ನಿಯಮವನ್ನು ಅದು ಬರೆಯದ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳಿಂದ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"Naive rule and its repair","headingKn":"ಸರಳ ನಿಯಮ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ದುರಸ್ತಿ","headers":["Rule","Naive version","Repair"],"rows":[["protected paths","set intersection of strings","normalise separators, dots and case"],["tests before completion","ran and exit 0","bind to the code revision"],["approval","an approval exists","right target, recorded before the action"],["severity","read from the run report","read from reviewed policy"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"ic_2.py","headingEn":"Naive and stronger checkers and the gate","headingKn":"ಸರಳ ಮತ್ತು ಬಲವಾದ checkers ಮತ್ತು gate","descEn":"naive_protected compares exact strings while normalised_protected normalises separators, dots and case and treats a directory as covering its contents. revision_tests requires the tested revision to equal the code revision. bound_approval needs the right target and a time before the action. gate reads severities from a table passed in by the caller.","descKn":"naive_protected ನಿಖರ ಸ್ಟ್ರಿಂಗ್‌ಗಳನ್ನು ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, normalised_protected ವಿಭಜಕಗಳು, ಚುಕ್ಕೆಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಕೇಸ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಿಸಿ ಡೈರೆಕ್ಟರಿ ತನ್ನ ವಿಷಯವನ್ನು ಆವರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂದು ಪರಿಗಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. revision_tests ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿದ revision ಕೋಡ್ revision ಗೆ ಸಮನಾಗಿರಬೇಕು. bound_approval ಸರಿಯಾದ ಗುರಿ ಮತ್ತು ಕ್ರಿಯೆಗೆ ಮುನ್ನದ ಸಮಯ ಬೇಕು. gate ಕರೆದವರು ನೀಡಿದ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕದಿಂದ ತೀವ್ರತೆಗಳನ್ನು ಓದುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"PROTECTED = ["deploy/release.py", "deploy/"]


def naive_protected(run):
    return not (set(run["protected_paths"]) & set(run["changed_paths"]))


def normalised_protected(run):
    def norm(p):
        return posixpath.normpath(p.replace("\\", "/")).lower()
    prot = [norm(p) for p in run["protected_paths"]]
    for c in map(norm, run["changed_paths"]):
        for p in prot:
            if c == p or c.startswith(p.rstrip("/") + "/"):
                return False
    return True


def naive_tests(run):
    return run["tests_ran"] and run["test_exit_code"] == 0


def revision_tests(run):
    return run["tests_ran"] and run["test_exit_code"] == 0 and run.get("tests_revision") == run.get("code_revision")


def naive_approval(run):
    return run["approval"] is not None and run["approval"]["approved"] is True


def bound_approval(run):
    a = run["approval"]
    return (a is not None and a["approved"] is True and a["target"] == run["target"] and a["at"] < run["action_at"])


def question_assumption(run):
    return not (set(run["unresolved"]) & set(run["assumed"]))


def semantic_assumption(run):
    norm = lambda s: " ".join(s.lower().replace("?", "").split())
    return not ({norm(q) for q in run["unresolved"]} & {norm(a) for a in run["assumed"]})


def gate(results, severity_table):
    return all(st == "pass" or severity_table[name] != "block" for name, st in results)"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"ic_2.py","headingEn":"main(): six experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಆರು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs each naive and stronger checker on adversarial inputs and compares a trusted severity table with a downgraded one.","descKn":"main() ಪ್ರತಿ ಸರಳ ಮತ್ತು ಬಲವಾದ checker ಅನ್ನು ಪ್ರತಿಕೂಲ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಓಡಿಸಿ ವಿಶ್ವಾಸಾರ್ಹ ತೀವ್ರತೆ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕವನ್ನು ಇಳಿಸಿದ್ದರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def section(t):
    print(f"\n--- {t} ---")


def main():
    section("1. Genuinely checking: protected-path matching against nine spellings of a changed path")
    base = {"protected_paths": ["deploy/release.py", "deploy/"]}
    spellings = ["deploy/release.py", "./deploy/release.py", "deploy//release.py", "deploy\\release.py", "DEPLOY/release.py", "src/../deploy/release.py", "deploy/other.py", "deploy", "src/app.py"]
    for sp in spellings:
        run = dict(base, changed_paths=[sp])
        print(f"{sp:28} naive says clean={naive_protected(run)!s:5} normalised says clean={normalised_protected(run)!s:5}")
    print("the naive set intersection only caught the exact string; normalising separators, '.' and '..' and case flagged every spelling of the release script and everything under the deploy directory; the bare name 'deploy' was flagged as well because normalising strips the trailing slash, so a file that happens to be named deploy would be a false positive, and a case-insensitive match would be wrong on a case-sensitive filesystem")

    section("2. Genuinely checking: tests that ran, but before the final edit")
    runs = {"fresh": dict(tests_ran=True, test_exit_code=0, tests_revision="r2", code_revision="r2"), "stale": dict(tests_ran=True, test_exit_code=0, tests_revision="r1", code_revision="r2"),
            "failed": dict(tests_ran=True, test_exit_code=1, tests_revision="r2", code_revision="r2")}
    for name, run in runs.items():
        print(f"{name:7} naive passes={bool(naive_tests(run))!s:5} revision-aware passes={bool(revision_tests(run))}")
    print("a green run from before the last edit satisfied the naive rule; tying the evidence to the revision refused it, and the revision label itself must come from a trusted runner")

    section("3. Genuinely checking: approval chronology and target binding")
    cases = {"approved before, right target": dict(approval={"approved": True, "target": "prod-eu", "at": 5}, target="prod-eu", action_at=10),
             "approved after the action": dict(approval={"approved": True, "target": "prod-eu", "at": 12}, target="prod-eu", action_at=10),
             "approved a different target": dict(approval={"approved": True, "target": "staging", "at": 5}, target="prod-eu", action_at=10), "no approval": dict(approval=None, target="prod-eu", action_at=10)}
    for name, run in cases.items():
        print(f"{name:30} naive passes={bool(naive_approval(run))!s:5} bound passes={bool(bound_approval(run))}")
    print("the naive rule accepted approval that came late and approval for another target; the bound rule needs the right target recorded before the action, and the approval record must come from a trusted source, not from the agent's own notes")

    section("4. Genuinely measuring: uncertainty detection by exact string versus normalised text")
    pairs = [(["Which production region?"], ["Which production region?"]), (["Which production region?"], ["which production region"]), (["Which production region?"], ["The region is probably eu-west."]), ([], ["anything"])]
    for q, a in pairs:
        run = dict(unresolved=q, assumed=a)
        print(f"question {q!s:32} assumption {a!s:34} exact passes={question_assumption(run)!s:5} normalised passes={semantic_assumption(run)}")
    print("the exact comparison missed a case-and-punctuation variant; both missed a paraphrased assumption, so detecting assumptions made without asking needs more than string matching and this rule is only a hint")

    section("5. Genuinely checking: severity from a trusted file versus the agent's own report")
    results = [("no-protected-writes", "fail"), ("ask-before-assuming", "fail")]
    trusted = {"no-protected-writes": "block", "ask-before-assuming": "warn"}
    forged = {"no-protected-writes": "info", "ask-before-assuming": "warn"}
    print("trusted severities -> release allowed:", gate(results, trusted))
    print("severity downgraded to info by the agent's report -> release allowed:", gate(results, forged))
    print("the failing result is identical in both calls; only the severity source changed, so severities must be read from reviewed policy and never from the run being judged")

    section("6. Genuinely checking: a high score hiding a block failure")
    scores = {"all pass": [("a", "pass")] * 10, "one block fails": [("a", "pass")] * 9 + [("protected", "fail")]}
    sev = {"a": "info", "protected": "block"}
    for name, res in scores.items():
        print(f"{name:16} score {sum(s == 'pass' for _, s in res) / len(res):.0%} gate allowed {gate(res, sev)}")
    print("the same 90 percent score can be a pass or a block depending on which rule failed")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
