[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Reviewer Agent (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"Reviewer Agent (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: a five-dimension rubric with one scorer per dimension, a verdict engine with a hard-fail rule and two demonstration cases. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind the reviewer agent (rubric, hard-fail rule, independent evidence and isolation), not the real software, and the reviewer is a deterministic stub reading structured evidence and no language model is involved, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. Only part of this module's source was supplied: Part 2 was pasted in full, while Parts 1 and 3 arrived only as small fragments (a progress checklist and closing summaries), and the original main.py was not provided. The lessons are built from Part 2 and those fragments, and the labs are our own implementation. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: ಪ್ರತಿ ಆಯಾಮಕ್ಕೆ ಒಂದು scorer ಇರುವ ಐದು-ಆಯಾಮದ rubric, hard-fail ನಿಯಮ ಇರುವ ತೀರ್ಪು ಎಂಜಿನ್ ಮತ್ತು ಎರಡು ಪ್ರದರ್ಶನ ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು reviewer agent (rubric, hard-fail ನಿಯಮ, ಸ್ವತಂತ್ರ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕತೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು reviewer ರಚನಾತ್ಮಕ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ ಓದುವ ನಿರ್ಣಾಯಕ ಬದಲಿ ಮತ್ತು ಯಾವುದೇ ಭಾಷಾ ಮಾದರಿ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ ಮಾಡ್ಯೂಲ್‌ನ ಮೂಲದ ಒಂದು ಭಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ ಒದಗಿಸಲಾಗಿತ್ತು: ಭಾಗ 2 ಪೂರ್ಣವಾಗಿ ಅಂಟಿಸಲಾಗಿತ್ತು, ಭಾಗ 1 ಮತ್ತು 3 ಸಣ್ಣ ತುಣುಕುಗಳಾಗಿ ಮಾತ್ರ ಬಂದವು (ಪ್ರಗತಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲನಾ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮುಕ್ತಾಯ ಸಾರಾಂಶಗಳು), ಮತ್ತು ಮೂಲ main.py ಒದಗಿಸಲಿಲ್ಲ. lessons ಭಾಗ 2 ಮತ್ತು ಆ ತುಣುಕುಗಳಿಂದ ನಿರ್ಮಿತ, ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"The Builder Should Not Mark Its Own Work","textKn":"Builder ತನ್ನ ಕೆಲಸಕ್ಕೆ ತಾನೇ ಅಂಕ ನೀಡಬಾರದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"A Rubric With a Hard-Fail Rule","headingKn":"Hard-Fail ನಿಯಮ ಇರುವ Rubric","bodyEn":"The system that builds a change should not be the only judge of it. The verification gate checks deterministic evidence; a reviewer judges problem fit, scope discipline, assumptions, verification quality and handoff readiness, each scored 0, 1 or 2 with a finding. This part builds the five scorers and the verdict engine, runs a clean change and a change that passes its tests while solving the wrong problem, and counts all 243 possible score combinations.","bodyKn":"ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುವ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆ ಅದರ ಏಕೈಕ ನ್ಯಾಯಾಧೀಶ ಆಗಬಾರದು. ಪರಿಶೀಲನಾ gate ನಿರ್ಣಾಯಕ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ; reviewer ಸಮಸ್ಯೆ ಹೊಂದಾಣಿಕೆ, ವ್ಯಾಪ್ತಿ ಶಿಸ್ತು, ಊಹೆಗಳು, ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಗುಣಮಟ್ಟ ಮತ್ತು ಹಸ್ತಾಂತರ ಸಿದ್ಧತೆ ನಿರ್ಣಯಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದಕ್ಕೂ finding ಜೊತೆ 0, 1 ಅಥವಾ 2. ಈ ಭಾಗ ಐದು scorers ಮತ್ತು ತೀರ್ಪು ಎಂಜಿನ್ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ, ಸ್ವಚ್ಛ ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಮತ್ತು ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ ಪಾಸ್ ಆಗಿ ತಪ್ಪು ಸಮಸ್ಯೆ ಬಗೆಹರಿಸುವ ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಓಡಿಸಿ, ಎಲ್ಲಾ 243 ಸಾಧ್ಯ ಅಂಕ ಸಂಯೋಜನೆಗಳನ್ನು ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Five Scorers, One Verdict","headingKn":"ಐದು Scorers, ಒಂದು ತೀರ್ಪು","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">Five scorers, one verdict</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">five scorers</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">0, 1 or 2 each</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">total /10</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">sum of scores</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">any zero</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">hard fail</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">pass / soft / hard</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">verdict</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">a zero outvotes the total</text></svg>","captionEn":"A zero in any dimension is a hard fail.","captionKn":"ಯಾವುದೇ ಆಯಾಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಸೊನ್ನೆ hard fail."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The rubric","headingKn":"Rubric","headers":["Dimension","0","2"],"rows":[["problem_fit","problem unsolved","requirement addressed"],["scope_discipline","unauthorised changes","within scope"],["assumptions","none recorded","recorded"],["verification_quality","gate did not pass","tests match the requirement"],["handoff_readiness","no next action","next action and evidence"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"rv_1.py","headingEn":"Scorers and the verdict engine","headingKn":"Scorers ಮತ್ತು ತೀರ್ಪು ಎಂಜಿನ್","descEn":"Each scorer returns a score and a finding from structured evidence, defaulting to the unsuccessful reading when a key is missing. verdict checks every score is exactly an int from 0 to 2, then returns hard_fail for any zero or a total below 5, soft_fail for 5 or 6, and pass otherwise.","descKn":"ಪ್ರತಿ scorer ರಚನಾತ್ಮಕ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯದಿಂದ ಅಂಕ ಮತ್ತು finding ಮರಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಕೀಲಿ ಕಾಣೆಯಾದಾಗ ವಿಫಲ ಓದುವಿಕೆ ಡೀಫಾಲ್ಟ್. verdict ಪ್ರತಿ ಅಂಕ ನಿಖರವಾಗಿ 0 ರಿಂದ 2 ರ int ಎಂದು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ, ಯಾವುದೇ ಸೊನ್ನೆ ಅಥವಾ 5 ಕ್ಕಿಂತ ಕಡಿಮೆ ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ hard_fail, 5 ಅಥವಾ 6 ಕ್ಕೆ soft_fail ಮತ್ತು ಉಳಿದದ್ದಕ್ಕೆ pass ಮರಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def problem_fit(d):
    if not d.state.get("solves_requested_problem", False):
        return 0, "The original problem remains unsolved."
    if not d.state.get("covers_all_requirements", False):
        return 1, "The task is only partially satisfied."
    return 2, "The implementation addresses the stated task."


def scope_discipline(d):
    if d.state.get("unauthorized_changes"):
        return 0, "Unauthorised files were changed."
    if d.state.get("scope_expansion_pending"):
        return 1, "A scope expansion awaits approval."
    return 2, "Changes stay within scope."


def assumptions(d):
    return (2, "Assumptions are listed.") if d.assumptions else (0, "No assumptions are recorded.")


def verification_quality(d):
    if not d.verification.get("passed", False):
        return 0, "The verification gate did not pass."
    if not d.feedback.get("tests_match_requirement", False):
        return 1, "The gate passed but the tests do not match the requirement."
    return 2, "Passing tests cover the requirement."


def handoff_readiness(d):
    if not d.handoff.get("next_action"):
        return 0, "No next action."
    if not d.handoff.get("evidence_paths"):
        return 1, "Next action without evidence references."
    return 2, "Next action and evidence are present."


SCORERS = {"problem_fit": problem_fit, "scope_discipline": scope_discipline, "assumptions": assumptions, "verification_quality": verification_quality, "handoff_readiness": handoff_readiness}


def verdict(scores):
    for k in DIMENSIONS:
        if k not in scores:
            raise ValueError(f"missing dimension {k}")
        v = scores[k]
        if type(v) is not int or not 0 <= v <= 2:
            raise ValueError(f"{k} must be an int from 0 to 2")
    total = sum(scores[k] for k in DIMENSIONS)
    if any(scores[k] == 0 for k in DIMENSIONS) or total < 5:
        return total, "hard_fail"
    return total, "soft_fail" if total <= 6 else "pass"


def review(d):
    dims = {k: dict(zip(("score", "finding"), SCORERS[k](d))) for k in DIMENSIONS}
    total, v = verdict({k: dims[k]["score"] for k in DIMENSIONS})
    return {"total": total, "verdict": v, "dimensions": dims}"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"rv_1.py","headingEn":"main(): five experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಐದು ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() reviews two cases, probes the hard-fail rule, enumerates all 243 combinations, feeds the verdict engine four bad scores and round-trips a report through JSON.","descKn":"main() ಎರಡು ಪ್ರಕರಣ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ, hard-fail ನಿಯಮ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ, ಎಲ್ಲಾ 243 ಸಂಯೋಜನೆ ಎಣಿಸಿ, ತೀರ್ಪು ಎಂಜಿನ್‌ಗೆ ನಾಲ್ಕು ತಪ್ಪು ಅಂಕ ನೀಡಿ, ವರದಿಯನ್ನು JSON ಮೂಲಕ round-trip ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: a clean change and a wrong-problem change")
    for name, d in (("clean", clean()), ("wrong problem", wrong_problem())):
        r = review(d)
        print(f"{name:14} gate passed={d.verification['passed']!s:5} total={r['total']}/10 verdict={r['verdict']}")
        print("   ", {k: v["score"] for k, v in r["dimensions"].items()})
    print("the wrong-problem change had a passing verification gate and still failed review: its total was 7 of 10, but a zero in problem fit forces hard_fail, so the high total could not outvote the one dimension that matters most")

    section("2. Genuinely checking: the hard-fail rule against the total")
    s = {k: 2 for k in DIMENSIONS}
    print("all twos                         :", verdict(s))
    print("problem_fit zero, others two     :", verdict(dict(s, problem_fit=0)))
    print("everything one (total 5)         :", verdict({k: 1 for k in DIMENSIONS}))
    print("two dimensions zero, others one  :", verdict(dict({k: 1 for k in DIMENSIONS}, problem_fit=0, assumptions=0)))
    print("a single zero gave hard_fail with a total of 8, and a total of 5 with no zeros was a soft_fail, so the verdict depends on both the sum and the minimum")

    section("3. Genuinely measuring: all 243 possible score combinations")
    c = Counter(verdict(dict(zip(DIMENSIONS, combo)))[1] for combo in itertools.product((0, 1, 2), repeat=5))
    print(dict(c), "| total combinations:", sum(c.values()))
    print("pass needs every dimension at 1 or 2 and a total of at least 7; only", c["pass"], "of 243 combinations pass, and", c["hard_fail"], "are hard fails, so most of the score space is a rejection")

    section("4. Genuinely checking: bad scores are rejected, booleans included")
    for label, sc in (("True instead of 1", dict(s, problem_fit=True)), ("score 3", dict(s, problem_fit=3)), ("score 1.0", dict(s, problem_fit=1.0)), ("missing dimension", {k: 2 for k in DIMENSIONS[:-1]})):
        try:
            verdict(sc)
            print(f"{label:20} accepted")
        except ValueError as e:
            print(f"{label:20} rejected: {e}")
    print("True is an int in Python and would have counted as 1, so the type is checked exactly; a verdict engine that accepted it could turn a boolean flag into a rubric score by accident")

    section("5. Genuinely checking: the report is serialisable evidence")
    out = json.dumps(review(wrong_problem()), indent=2)
    back = json.loads(out)
    print("round trip equal:", back == review(wrong_problem()), "| keys:", sorted(back), "| problem_fit:", back["dimensions"]["problem_fit"])
    print("the report keeps the score and the finding side by side, so a builder can act on 'The original problem remains unsolved.' and a later session can see why the change was rejected; these findings are fixed strings chosen by the stub, not an analysis of any code")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
